<h2>7. Input Validations, Security & Quality Audit Checklist</h2>
<p>The entire platform has been audited against 25 automated end-to-end test cases (<code>npm run audit</code>):</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Email Validation:</strong> Evaluated using regex (<code>/^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/</code>), normalized to lowercase, and checked for uniqueness before saving.</li>
  <li><strong>Phone Validation:</strong> Validates 10-digit Indian mobile numbers (<code>/^[6-9]\d{9}$/</code>), automatically stripping country codes (+91), spaces, and dashes.</li>
  <li><strong>Password Security:</strong> Enforces minimum 6 characters and hashes passwords using <code>bcryptjs</code> with 10 salt rounds.</li>
  <li><strong>Duplicate Prevention:</strong> Enforces unique email on <code>users</code>, unique compound index on <code>applications</code> (<code>{ taskId: 1, volunteerId: 1 }</code>), and unique NGO registration numbers.</li>
  <li><strong>Task Integrity & Category Enforcement:</strong> Strictly validates the 6 mandatory categories (Education, Food distribution, Environment, Elder support, Disaster support, Community service) and enforces positive integers for volunteers and hours.</li>
  <li><strong>Role-Based Access Control:</strong> Uses signed JSON Web Tokens (JWT) with <code>protect</code>, <code>requireVolunteer</code>, <code>requireNGO</code>, and <code>requireAdmin</code> middleware.</li>
  <li><strong>CRUD Completeness:</strong> NGOs can Create, Read, Update (inline status and modal edit), and Delete their published tasks with cascading clean-up of associated records.</li>
</ul>

<h2>8. System Administrator Access & Governance Architecture</h2>
<p><strong>Root Cause of Previous "Access Denied":</strong> An administrator (<code>role: 'admin'</code>) is a platform superuser, not an individual volunteer or a single NGO. When logging in, the frontend previously redirected all non-NGO accounts to <code>/volunteer-dashboard.html</code>, which is protected by the <code>requireVolunteer</code> middleware. Because the admin has role <code>'admin'</code> and does not possess a volunteer profile, the backend correctly enforced role boundaries and rejected the call with <code>403 Forbidden (Access denied: Volunteers only)</code>.</p>
<p><strong>Solution Implemented:</strong></p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Dedicated Superuser Portal:</strong> Created <code>admin-dashboard.html</code> with platform metrics, user directory, partner NGO registry, and all community tasks.</li>
  <li><strong>Superuser REST API:</strong> Created <code>routes/adminRoutes.js</code> protected by <code>requireAdmin</code> for platform overview (<code>GET /api/admin/overview</code>), user management (<code>GET/DELETE /api/admin/users</code>), and task moderation (<code>GET/PUT/DELETE /api/admin/tasks</code>).</li>
  <li><strong>Intelligent Role Routing:</strong> On login, administrators are automatically routed directly to the <code>Admin Portal</code>, and the navbar renders a dedicated <code>ADMINISTRATOR</code> badge and shortcut button.</li>
</ul>

